id: pm-fnx3np
title: Remove unpatched braces recursion vulnerability from file matching
description: "GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm / CVE-2026-93687: braces 3.0.3 reaches production through fast-glob 3.3.3 and micromatch 4.0.8. The mandatory complete audit rejects this tree. No patched braces version is published. Replace the glob implementation while retaining SDK linked file semantics and complete quality censuses."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[4]: dependencies,glob,sdk,security
created_at: "2026-10-03T01:35:10.144Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-03T02:46:48.413Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-03T02:42:02.954Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-03T02:42:02.954Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Zero full audit findings; no installed braces or micromatch path; real deeply nested input succeeds without stack overflow; brace and extglob matching retains dot files and absolute or nested relative anchoring; literal directories stay excluded; complete source census and coverage gates pass
goal: continuously enforced software supply-chain trust
objective: Remove recursive vulnerable brace expansion from production SDK matching and repository source censuses
value: Agent-supplied file patterns remain usable without a vulnerable transitive parser or changes to link identity
why_now: A newly reviewed advisory blocks the mandatory complete dependency audit during the same reviewed security delivery
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: Replace fast-glob with tinyglobby throughout SDK matching and repository censuses. Explicitly preserve file-only directory behavior and invocation anchoring; retain a real nested-pattern regression and required native Windows coverage.
expected_result: No vulnerable braces or micromatch dependency path; nested patterns cannot exhaust the old recursion stack; file matching and complete source census contracts retain their behavior.
actual_result: Full and production audits report zero advisories. All 9631 source tests pass with exact 100/100/100/100 and twelve independently recorded counts. Real Node/Bun CLI and published SDK entrypoint consumers plus nine-package npm/npx/bunx and 89-command acceptance pass. Native exact-head checks precede merge; immutable publication remains a separate release-health obligation.
component: sdk/linked-artifacts
